Commit:     john@thunderbird.net <john@thunderbird.net>
CommitDate: Fri Jun 26 10:53:49 2026 +0000

    Bug 1806770 - Use 0 for the null IMAP UID, rather than 0xffffffff (nsMsgKey_None). r=mkmelin

    This patch tidies up a few places where nsMsgKey_None (0xffffffff) was being used where there should really have been a zero UID.
    Just another quirk of using message keys and UIDs interchangably.
    I could have redefined ImapUid_None as 0 instead of removing it, but I think the explicit use of 0 is clearer, especially in the context of IMAP UIDs as described in the RFCs.

    Differential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D307992

